
users(  user_id int  not null PK
        email varchar not null UK
        displayname not null varchar )


movies (   movie_id int not null PK
          title varchar not null
          is_available varchar not null default 'Y'
          release_year int not null )


The relationship between ratings and users is handled differently: 
when a user account is deleted, ON DELETE CASCADE removes 
that user's ratings along with them, 
since a rating with no rater isn't a meaningful record, 
and most privacy-driven account deletions 
expect associated activity to go too.
For the foreign key from ratings to movies, 
this makes ON DELETE RESTRICT the right choice — 
the application should never be able to physically 
remove a movie that still has ratings attached,
 forcing any true deletion through the soft-delete path instead(is_available)
ratings(  rating_id int PK
         user_id int not null FK 
         movie_id int not null  FK
        score   int not null default 0
         rated_at date not null
    FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(user_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    FOREIGN KEY (movie_id) REFERENCES movies(movie_id) ON DELETE RESTRICT
        )

   
genres (   genre_id  int not null PK
           name UK varchar not null
        )

movie_id	CASCADE	A junction row only exists to say "this movie belongs to this genre."
 Once the movie itself is gone, that association is meaningless — 
 there's nothing left for it to describe. 
 Cascading avoids leaving orphaned rows that reference a 
 nonexistent movie.
 One caveat since movies table uses soft-deletes (is_available) 
 rather than hard deletes, movie_id's ON DELETE CASCADE will rarely fire
  in practice — it's really there as a safety net for the 
  rare hard-delete
genre_id	RESTRICT	Genres are reference/lookup data 
(Action, Drama, Comedy), and are almost always shared across many movies.
 If someone tries to delete a genre that's still tagged on movies,
  you want that blocked 
movie_genres( movie_id int not null PK, FK
              genre_id int not null PK, FK
     FOREIGN KEY (movie_id) REFERENCES movies(movie_id)
        ON DELETE CASCADE,
    FOREIGN KEY (genre_id) REFERENCES genres(genre_id)
        ON DELETE RESTRICT)